  "note": "Tests using named resources and joint energy and reserve offers did not reproduce the official reserve price (RSVPR). When scheduled reserve met the requirement, the marginal demand-response offer reproduced RSVPR to the centavo. When scheduled reserve fell below the market requirement (MKT_REQT), the official price exceeded every public offer. A model that forced the full requirement was infeasible for those hours. This indicates an administered shortage price that is absent from the public offers. Fixing energy dispatch to the observed schedule (DIPCEF) and registered capacity (CAPEG) produced the same result. The model therefore keeps its current approximation and shows both the unmet requirement and official price.",
